Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA  Patient with infiltrating carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    GRADE II III  PRESENT AT LATERAL AND INFERIOR INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  30    COMEDO AND CRIBIFORM TYPES  PRESENT AT DEEP and LATERAL INKED RESECTION MARGINS  NOTE  The carcinoma is 2 5cm in largest dimension  Four of twenty one lymph nodes identified are positive for metastatic carcinoma  One lymph node demonstrates extracapsular extension  The  re excision of close margin  contains carcinoma  Several of the foci of carcinoma in situ at the margins are suspicious for micro invasion but cautery artifact precludes optimal assessment  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left lateral breast   is a 9 x 6 x 2cm piece of breast tissue with overlying skin ellipse  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  containing a well healed scar  A double suture marks the superior end of this specimen and a single suture designates the medial portion  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  white tan  firm  mass with a stellate shape  measuring about REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm  closely approaching the lateral margin within less than 0 1cm  Representative section of lateral margin frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  SECTION CODE  AandB  lateral margin  radial C  section where firm mass come close to deep margin  0 4cm away grossly D  medial margin  next to stitch with fibrous tissue E  closest extent of hard nodule to superior margin  just lateral to skin ellipse F  inferior margin  en face G  superior margin  en face  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  re excision   are fragments of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 2cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  all frozen as FX 2 and submitted as H  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a 6 x 5 x 4 0cm axillary node dissection with fibrofatty tissue and lymph nodes  About 21 possible lymph nodes are identified none grossly positive 