  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Blue dyed region with hemorrhagic area entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Few indurated areas from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan red lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The attached adipose tissue is removed  and the specimen is serially sectioned at approximately 0 2cm increments  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Less than 10  of the in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Definite invasive tumor is not identified on the tissue sections for receptor immunohistochemistry  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The invasive tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The invasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The invasive tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by