Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 32 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast lump with abnormal mammogram  Short suture superior  Long suture lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  INTRADUCTAL  95   AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL  5   CARCINOMA ABUTTING INFERIOR INKED MARGIN  ER PR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY WILL BE REPORTED AS AN ADDENDUM  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN   LUMPECTOMY  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm lumpectomy specimen  oriented with a short suture at the superior margin and a long suture at the lateral margin  Entire surface is inked black and the inferior surface is again inked yellow  Sectioning of the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm round  white  firm and gritty nodule  0 2cm from the inferior resection margin  A representative portion is frozen as FX 1  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast   are two fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  of fibroadipose tissue with an unremarkable tan and yellow mottled cut surface  SECTION CODE A H  breast lump  entirely submitted  serially progressing lateral to medial   B and C represent posterior and anterior portion of one section  respectively  cassettes D and E represent the posterior and anterior portions of the adjacent section  respectively  The frozen section was taken from the section in cassette F   I J  additional inferior margin  towards anterior  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer status post Hodgkin s treatment  Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal carcinoma in situ by core biopsy   5  REMOVED_CASE_ID    FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS AND CALCIUM OXALATE CRYSTALS  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  SEE TABLE  1  NOTE  Both regions of calcifications correspond to areas of fibrocystic changes  The tumor cells stain for E cadherin  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor Size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Grade  2  Lymphatic Vessel Invasion  Not identified  Blood Vessel Invasion  Not identified  Margin of Invasive Carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for Receptors  Not Indicated  See prior report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    BREAST  LEFT   INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen s  were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 6 OF 6 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margins  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm cystic space containing a gray to tan yellow friable material  The cyst wall is gray pink  fibrous  and averages less than 0 1cm in thickness  The cystic structure focally abuts the postero inferior margin and comes to 1 0cm of the anterior  4 0cm of the superior  and more than 2cm of the medial and lateral margins  Abutting the cyst along the posterosuperior aspect  is a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm indurated gray white lobulated mass which comes to 0 5cm of the posterior  1 2cm of the inferior  1 3cm of the anterior  3 7cm of the superior  and 1 7cm of the lateral  and greater than 2cm of the medial margin  Along the anterosuperior aspect of the indurated lesion is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic space containing a soft tan brown substance  The space is consistent with previous biopsy site and is surrounded by focal bright yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The space comes to 0 3cm of the anterior  REMOVED_DATE of the superior  2 0cm of the inferior  1 4cm of the posterior  1 7cm of the lateral  and greater than 2cm of the medial margins  One of the localization wires is located in the tissue immediately medial to the indurated lesion and cavity  The second localization wire is located 1 2cm medial to the first wire  The cross sections are taken to breast imaging and radiographed  The remaining dense gray white fibrous tissue shows focal gritty areas  Representative section is submitted  from medial to lateral  as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region designated by second localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible calcification to superior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible calcifications   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area designated by localization wire  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire indurated lesion and representative hemorrhagic cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cystic structure  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative hemorrhagic cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible calcifications  NOTE  Please note radiographs accompany the specimen and are mapped according to tissue in the radiographs  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular portion of yellow fatty tissue  within which multiple tan pink candidate lymph nodes are identified  The candidate lymph nodes are submitted in entirety for frozen section as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two bisected candidate lymph nodes  both of which are inked   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple whole candidate lymph nodes and one bisected lymph node  inked black   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow pink irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue  with a stitch designating the new margin  inked black   The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly yellow fatty cut surface  with focal yellow chalky areas  No lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  2  SENTINEL NODES  BIOPSY  CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORK UP  Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on 