ay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 97 at 15 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fibroadipose tissue overlaid by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm skin ellipse  designated by a long suture for the lateral margin  a short suture for the superior margin and a double stitch suture for the the deep margin  The specimen is inked blue laterally  red   medially  black   superiorly  and yellow   inferiorly  The skin contains a 2 5cm healed surgical scar  The specimen is sectioned to reveal two areas with fat necrosis consistent with previous biopsy sites  The first biopsy site is more superficial and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The fat necrosis extends focally to the superior resection margin  The second biopsy site is deeper in the tissue and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The fat necrosis in the second biopsy site extends focally to the lateral resection margin and 1 7cm to the deep resection margin  The adjacent breast tissue is fibrofatty and focally cystic  Section code  A D  representative sections of the f