Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 43 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  OCCUPYING THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FEW FOCI IN THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  and designated as  L breast  stitch superior   is a 30 x 17 x 5 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and a 4 0cm linear scar  8cm lateral to the nipple  A stitch designates the superior aspect of the specimen  The attached axillary tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Deep to the skin scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity surrounded by a rim of ill defined tan yellow  fibrous tissue  It abuts the overlying skin and is 0 8cm from the nearest deep resection margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined tan white rubbery area located 4 0cm lateral to the biopsy cavity  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  The axillary nodes range in size from 0 4cm to 1 7cm in greatest diameter and are rubbery and tan pink  Section Code  A  cavity with skin margin B  deep margin C E  representative sections of the mass F H  nodular areas I and J  axillary nodes Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
