Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 12 CLINICAL DATA  72 year old woman undergoing excision of a right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  DISPLAYING BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CHARACTERISTICS  SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  OCCUPYING DUCTS IN SIX OF TEN SECTIONS  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of pro