or estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm unoriented piece of fibroadipose tissue containing a guide wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty parenchyma  Entirely submitted in cassettes A through J with the area including the thick segment of the wire in cassettes E and F  Received fresh in two separate containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen  4 x 17 x 22cm  containing a REMOVED_DATE x 18cm skin ellipse which includes a 3 x 3cm slightly eccentric nipple  The deep margin of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a 2 x 2 x 2 5cm firm  ill defined  tan pink area which measures 1 5cm from the closest  deep  margin  Representative section of the tumor with the closest  deep  margin is submitted in cassette K  Representative areas of the tumor in L through N  Representative unremarkable breast away from the mass are submitted in O and P  The axillary tail measures 5 x 7 x 10cm in overall dimensions  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes Q through T  Labeled  