Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 11 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right breast needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON THE GROSS SPECIMEN  PRESENT AT INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1    CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM INVASIVE CARCINOMA  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED SURFACE  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen SectionLab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast biopsy specimen containing a 1 5cm firm  tan  ill defined nodule approaching an inked margin  Representative with margin is frozen as FX 1  submitted in A  Tumor with margin in B  representative tumor in C and D  representative surrounding in E  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
