Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  01 MAY 96 at 18 45 CLINICAL DATA  31 year old female with breast biopsy x 2 revealing infiltrating ductal carcinoma with   margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU OCCUPYING 4 OF 4 BLOCKS OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MEDIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  MULTIPLE PAPILLOMAS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 21 OF 21 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL TISSUE    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 96 at 14 45                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Right breast with axillary contents  consists of a modified radical mastectomy having an overall measurement of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and weighing 480 grams  Also submitted with the mastectomy is an ellipse of skin containing areolar and nipple  This portion of skin containing the areolar measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  There are two sutures on the ellipse of skin  one with a long suture  one half of the ellipse and short suture on the other half of the ellipse  However this specimen has not been oriented as to where the suture lies  There is a healed surgical incisional scar measuring 2 0cm located on the medial aspect of the skin ellipse  The remainder of the skin ellipse and nipple is unremarkable  The specimen has been inked and sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity and surrounding firm tissue  The biopsy cavity measures 1 5cm in diameter and is located in the medial one half of the breast  The biopsy cavity comes to within 0 2cm of the deep inked surgical resection margin and 2 5cm from the medial resection margin  Surrounding the biopsy cavity is a firm area of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and appears to contain calcium flecks  This firmer area is located away from the deep surgical resection margin  The remainder of the breast tissue has been sampled to reveal unremarkable fibrous breast parenchyma and unremarkable adipose tissue  Section Code  A  section through ellipse of skin showing surgical scar  B  section through nipple and areolar  C  medial resection margin  D G  biopsy cavity and adjacent firm tissue lesion  submitted in toto  showing closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin  black ink   H I  two sections through firm areas located in the upper outer quadrant  no discrete lesion  fibrous tissue  J N  lymph nodes  Labeled  Additional axillary tissue  right breast  consist of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Individual lymph nodes from this specimen are submitted entirely in cassette O  Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
