Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 32 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   REEXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT IN THE WALL OF THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NOTE  The margins appear free of ductal carcinoma in situ  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  21  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 36                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen was inked in the following manner  medial and lateral margins are black  superior margin is green  deep margin is blue  anterior margin is red  inferior margin is yellow  The specimen was serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with a hemorrhagic ring  An area of increased consistency is found around the cavity that is 0 5cm from the closest  medial  margin  Representative sections are frozen as FX 1 and FX 2  Section Code  A  FX 1  biopsy cavity including closest  mediosuperior  resection margin B  FX 2  biopsy cavity  including closest  mediosuperior  resection margin C  Deep margin D  Inferior margin E  Biopsy cavity and superior margin F  Additional margins  including biopsy cavity  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name