cessed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Wide excision  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm fragment of breast with a 4 x 0 3cm overlying skin ellipse  which displays a 0 4cm long central scar  Two sutures  one long  one short  are present and provide orientation  The specimen is inked in black and the inferior aspect is additionally inked in yellow  A REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm blood filled cavity is present 1 1cm deep to the skin and approaches to 1cm of the deep margin  The cavity is lined by firm  and focally hard  yellow tissue  Inferior to the cavity  extending to the inferior resection margin  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm rubbery  white region  Superior to the cavity is soft to rubbery fibroadipose tissue  SECTION CODE  A   scar with underlying biopsy cavity B   lateral margin  inferior portion C   medial margin D through L   sections of the biopsy cavity and surrounding tissue  from lateral to medial  including rubbery white area  Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
