ed 1cm from the closest medial anterior margin  2cm from the posterior margin  and 3 5cm from the inferior margin  A 2nd area with some granularity and possibly fat necrosis is identified inferiorly to the previously described one and 0 2cm from the previously described area  The 2nd area is ill defined and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm and is located up to 0 2cm from the medial margin  1cm from the posterior margin  1cm from the superior margin  3cm from the inferior margin  0 8cm from the inferior margin and more than 2cm from the superior margin  The rest of the parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous areas from superior to inferior  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  both present in the area where the clip was identified and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the 1st area of nodularity  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the 2nd area of granularity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of grossly unremarkable breast tissue away from the lesion and inferior to the lesion  Received in formalin and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  additional right axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  containing candidate lymph nodes  Candidate lymph nodes are identified  measuring up to 0 4cm in largest dimension and are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm additional candidate lymph node is identified  bisected and submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The rest of the adipose tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 17   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 39 14PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally rev