Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels  including dermal lymphatics is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  are four nodules of adipose tissue  The first consists of an unoriented ellipse of unremarkable skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm nodule of adipose tissue with a grossly unremarkable white yellow cut surface  The remaining three nodules all consist of unremarkable adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Sectioning into these nodules discloses a diffusely firm texture cut surface and the absence of a discrete lesion  Representative section from the body of the first specimen is frozen as FX 1  which contains skin  submitted in C  The specimen is submitted for permanents as listed below  A  unoriented specimen REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse B  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm specimen C  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm specimen D  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm specimen Section code  Skin piece  A  one end B  other end C  frozen and body D  rest of body Specimen B  bisected and all in cassette E C  trisected and all in cassette F D  all in cassette G Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SKIN AND SUCUTIS  BREAST  LEFT   INVASIVE CARCINOMA PRESENT AT THE INKED EDGE OF THIS TISSUE FRAGMENT  NO OBVIOUS LYMPHATIC PLUGGING IS SEEN  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
