Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 41 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  1 5CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MASS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with sutures designating medial  double pin  and inferior  single pin   This specimen is inked black  the anterior margin double inked with yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm diameter firm area grossly abutting the anterior margin  Representative section of this margin is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of tissue are submitted entirely in cassettes A   M  proceeding laterally to medially  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  leftt breast  additional mass  are several fragments of yellow to pink fibroadipose tissue  one of which is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm with a long stitch marking the medial and short stitch marking the inferior aspect of the specimen  The anterior surface of this particular fragment is more fibrous than the posterior surface  The later consists mostly of yellow adipose tissue  The entire specimen is inked black  the anterior surface is double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm white firm mass located on the superior aspect of this specimen abutting against both the anterior and posterior resection surfaces  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes N through Q  The other fragments of fibroadipose tissue within the same specimen container are three pieces of unoriented fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Each fragment are submitted entirely in cassettes R through T  respectively  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA    MIXED PATTERN  EXTENSIVELY CLOSE TO AND PROBABLY INVOLVING ANTERIOR  YELLOW   MEDIAL  SECTION J  MARGIN  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST  SPECIMEN  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST   ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISIONAL BIOPS   report_end  , Unchecked.
