EINS Breast  Right  block G   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram right modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring 36 x 20 x 4cm  The axillary tail measures 12 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The overlying skin ellipse covers the majority of the anterior surface and measures 36 x 19cm  The areolar area measures 7 x 4cm  There is an undesignated suture which is arbitrarily  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  clock by the prosector  The margin is inked black and the rim of the anterior margin is inked blue  Sectioning reveals three distinct masses  Mass  1 is 5 1cm  tan white  granular  well circumbsribed  located in the mid inferior portion of the breast  and present 3cm from the deep margin and 1cm from the skin  Mass  2 is located 2 5cm superior lateral to the Mass  1  measures 4cm  and is present 3cm from the deep margin  Mass  3 is a firm 1 5cm well circumbscribed lesion in the axillary tail  The remainder of the breast tissue appears tan yellow  lobulated and unremarkable  The axillary tail contains multiple candidate lymph nodes ranging from 0 5cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Two of the largest nodes display a tan white  gritty cut surface  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Deep margin to mass  1  C  Mass  1  D  