 processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens  Labeled  left breast cancer  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral   is an oriented portion of breast  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm with an overlying ellipse of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  There is a longitudinal scar on the skin  measuring 2 5cm  There is short and long stitch present on the specimen  The deep margin is inked black  the superior margin is inked green  the inferior margin is inked red  and the anterior margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm  white  well defined nodule abutting the inferior deep margin  SECTION CODE  A B  medial margins of the specimen  Representative sections from medial to latera  including the well defined nodule  submitted in cassettes A through J  Labeled  left breast  additional medial tissue with the short stitch designating superior margin and the long stitch designating the new medial margin   is a portion of breast  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm with two stitch  one long and one short  The anterior portion is inked blue  the deep margin is inked black  the superior margin is inked green  and the inferior margin is inked red  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral  The entire tissue is quite firm and white  Entirely submitted in from medial to lateral in cassettes K through S  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE 