Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 18 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  95   WITH ASSOCIATED LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    AND SINGLE DUCT WITH DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The carcinoma is 1 1cm in greatest dimension  as measured from the slide   and it extends to a broad area of the resection margin  There is no evidence of vascular space invasion  The focus of ductal carcinoma in situ is surrounded by the invasive component of the tumor  Receptor studies are pending and will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Cooper Moore MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm excisional breast biopsy with accompanying specimen radiograph and localizing needle  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  white  gritty nodule  adjacent to the inked margin  The nodule is submitted entirely in A D and the remainder of this specimen in E H  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SUSPICIOUS NODULE TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 02 CLINICAL DATA  Breast cancer  plus additional calcification  Needle core biopsy revealed infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN DESIGNATED BY TWO SUTURES  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY   1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR  SUPERFICIAL  RESECTION MARGIN  AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   5   SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR MARGIN AND LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  3  RADIAL SCARS  4  COLLAGENOUS SPHENULOSIS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AT AN INKED SURFACE  2  RADIAL SCARS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  4  COLLAGENOUS SPHERULOSIS  BREAST  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 6 OF 14 LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Extra nodal tumor extension is present in 3 of the 6 positive nodes  Peri nodal lymphatic involvement is seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  mass   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five parts  Received in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy specimen with localizing wire in place and accompanying X ray film  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal scattered cystic structure ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through J  with area corresponding to calcification in cassettes A through D  Received in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch designating the superior margin and the long stitch designating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked entirely with black and additionally with yellow posteriorly  deep margin   and superiorly wi