tain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  excision of right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior yellow  inferior orange  lateral green  medial red  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white gritty stellate mass within the center of the specimen  more towards the medial side  The mass is approximately 0 4cm from the anterior margin  0 4cm from the superior medial margin and 1 0cm from the posterior and inferior margins  There is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan firm stellate mass adjacent to the larger mass  This smaller mass is located 0 2cm from the anterior margin and from the superior margin  The remaining breast tissue is approximately 80  fatty and 20  fibrous with focal areas of hemorrhage  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Mass to anterior margin C D  Mass to superior medial margin E  Smaller mass F  Tissue around the lesion with hemorrhage H G  Representative of breast away from lesion  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of adipose within which multiple tan pink lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 2cm to 5 0cm in greatest dimension  The largest lymph node has a tan white small cut surface with areas of necrosis and hemorrhage  Representative sections are submitted as follows  J N  Whole lymph nodes O P  Representative of the largest lymph node Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shave margin   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue which is entirely submitted in cassettes Q T  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT  AXILLARY CONTENTS   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXC BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 20 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammatory carcinoma  right breast  previous chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SMALL FOCUS  2  FIBROSIS  GLANDULAR ATROPHY  SCAR  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND MULTINUCLEATED FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  3  ELEVEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH SINUS HISTIOCYTOSIS  AND NESTS OF BENIGN APPEARING NEVOMELANOCYTES IN ONE LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The inked resection margins are negative for carcinoma  A single lymph node shows numerous benign appearing nests of nevomelanocytic cells  This may be observed rarely as an incidental finding  however  the degree of involvement of this lymph node suggests the possibility of metastasis from a blue nevus or other melanocytic proliferation  Drs  Lynn Duncan and Martin Mihm have reviewed the lymph node slides and concur with the interpretation  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 21                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  Right breast and axillary contents  is a 390 gm  23 x 15 x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 5cm skin ellipse containing a curved  2cm  well healed scar lateral to the areola  A long and a small black suture are attached to the specimen  designating the lateral and superior aspect  respectively  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing predominantly lobulated  yellow adipose tissue intermixed with gray white  fibrous breast parenchyma that is slightly firmer and with a gritty consistency in the region below the skin scar  The nipple and areola are unremarkable  The axillary adipose tissue is sectioned  revealing several tan pink  soft  grossly unremarkable lymph nodes measuring up to 1cm in greatest diameter  SECTION CODE  A B   breast and deep resection margin in the area underlying the scar C through G   breast parenchyma in the area underlying the scar H I   random sections from unremarkable breast J   nipple K   skin scar L M   axillary lymph nodes  Labeled  Right additional axillary tissue  is a 1 x 1 x 0 3cm piece of adipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a lymph node most of which has been replaced by fat  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in N  Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMB GEN SURGICAL   ACC 4 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST WITH AXILLA PART B  RIGHT ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
