ts of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five specimens  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right breast lump  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm oriented breast specimen  The superior half is inked in black  inferior half in blue and the anterior half is overinked in green  It is sectioned to reveal a white to gray  stellate area measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension and 0 4cm from the superior  closest  resection margin in the lateral half of the specimen  This area is submitted entirely in cassettes A through C with additional sections of the lateral half in D through F  Representative sections of the medial half are submitted in G and H  Labeled  additional superior margin  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating the superior aspect which is inked in black while the opposite inferior aspect is inked in blue  and a long stitch designating lateral aspect  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  representative sections are submitted lateral to medial in cassettes I through M  Labeled  final shaved margins  right breast  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm in aggregate  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  entirely submitted in cassettes N through R  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm in greatest dimension tan pink area which may represent a lymph node  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette S  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes T through Z  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   RESIDUAL CARCINOMA PRESENT  MARGINS GROSSLY NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  SUPERIOR  ADDITIONAL MARGINS   PART C  BREAST  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS  PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  PART E  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS    report_end  , Unchecked.
