rgin  The rest of the breast parenchyma contains approximately 20  tan white fibrous tissue and 80  tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No discrete mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire fibrotic area to include inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous tissue  lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous tissue  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  upper outer quadrant tissues that may represent lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock position  The overlying tan brown REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm skin ellipse contains a grossly unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm flatten nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  This specimen is serially sectioned along medial to lateral axis to reveal two fibrous scars  The first REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan white  stellate shaped fibrous scar in the outer lower quadrant grossly abuts the anterior inked margin and lies 1 0cm from the posterior inked margin  Approximately 4 5cm medial to this area there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink to tan white  stellate shaped fibrous scar present in the lower inner quadrant which lies 2 0cm from anterior inked margin and 0 4cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the first stellate scar is tan white and nodular  The intervening parenchyma between the 2 scars shows diffuse tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows minimal fibrous tissue  No discrete mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first fibrotic area to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tan white nodular breast parenchyma surrounding the first scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second tan white fibrotic area to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous tissue  upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous tissue  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissues that may represent lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  additional left mastectomy flap tissue  are four unoriented portions of tan brown skin ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Representative section is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  additional right mastectomy flap tissue  are two portions of unoriented tan brown skin which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative section is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A   RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2 AND  2A   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  There is no evidence of invasive carcinoma on the additional levels examined of the focus of extravasated mucin  Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E  SKIN  ADDITIONAL LEFT FLAP   EXCISION PART F  SKIN  ADDITIONAL RIGHT FLAP   EXCISION PART G  CRYOSTAT FROZEN  report_end  , Unchecked.
