e she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5 cm portion of tan yellow  lobulated adipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0 cm lymph node  which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  1A  1B  and 1C  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively   J N   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 cm simple mastectomy specimen with a suture at 12 o clock position  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2 cm nipple are unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue and posterior black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3 cm linear  tan white fibrotic scar  which lies 2 5cm from the anterior surface and 4cm from the posterior surface  The surrounding breast parenchyma is firm and nodular and feels gritty and so does the parenchyma lateral to the scar  in the outer upper and outer lower quadrants  The breast parenchyma medial to the scar is grossly unremarkable  A single possible lymph node  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  is identified  In the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 0 6cm fragment of tan yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue  which is unremarkable  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire tan white scar  located at the 12 o clock position   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast parenchyma adjacent to the scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of outer upper quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of