CRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm section of breast tissue  There is a long stitch marking the lateral position and short stitch marking the superior position  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior edge overinked in green  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular tan white gritty nodule in the inferior half of the specimen  This nodule to designated as nodule  1  This nodule abuts the posterior inferior margin   closest margin   There is also a small firm white nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in the superior half of the specimen  lateral to the first nodule  The nodule is designated as nodule  2  Nodule  2 comes to 0 4cm from the superior anterior margin  closest margin   Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  posterior inferior resection margin in relationship to nodule  1 with resection margin  closest margin  B D  area around posterior nodule  E  superior anterior margin in the relationship to nodule  2  with resection margin  closest margin   F  medial margin G  lateral margin Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  are two pieces of fatty tissue containing sentinel nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Each node is frozen as fx 1  and  2  The specimens are entirely submitted in cassettes H I  respectively  Resident  DAVID COON  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINELL NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURC