Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Paula Arnell  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Locally advanced right breast cancer status post neoadjuvant AC taxol chemo  Short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE AND NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE AND NOTE  SMALL CAPILLARY HEMANGIOMA  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 10 OUT OF 10 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  extensive  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the mass Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Note  Morphologically  the tumor s infiltrative pattern is reminiscent of lobular carcinoma  An e cadherin stain  however  reveals strong staining around the in situ and invasive components of the tumor  which in addition to a few areas where the invasive tumor s growth pattern is cribriform  are the basis for classifying the tumor as invasive ductal carcinoma  As the tumor is post therapy  the grading of the invasive and in situ components may not be entirely accurate  There is striking fibrosis within the tumor which is likely secondary to chemotherapy effect  The lymph nodes show marked therapy related fibrosis as well  The metastatic tumor within the lymph nodes consists of aggregates of tumor   0 2cm  and single cells scattered throughout the fibrotic stroma  Cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stains help confirm the presence of tumor cells within the more fibrotic lymph nodes  No definite extracapsular extension is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN FOUR OUT OF FOUR LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lymph nodes show significant fibrosis  consistent with chemotherapy effect  Cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stains confirm the presence of scattered tumor cells within the more fibrotic lymph nodes  There is tumor present within extranodal lymphatic vessels  but no definite extracapsular extension is identified  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right modified radical mastectomy  is a an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm axillary tail  The specimen is surfaced by an REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan pink areola  The areola comes to 1 8cm of the superior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unremarkable tan pink nipple which comes to 2 2cm of the closest inferior margin  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a fairly well defined  largely centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm indurated tan pink mass with several contiguous peripheral nodules predominantly along the inferior and medial aspects o