D_DATE x 2 6cm breast excision specimen with two needle guide wires in place  There is a short stitch marking the anterior position  a long stitch marking the lateral position  a bowtie marking the cephalad position  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm white nodule that is 0 6cm from the anterior superior margin  1 3cm from the posterior margin  1 1cm from the green inked superior margin  and 2cm from the yellow inked inferior margin  This is the area also enclosed by the guide wires  The remaining parenchyma is composed of yellow breast tissue and ill defined white fibrous tissue  It runs through the parenchyma and abuts the anterior and posterior margins in the medial end of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Lateral margin  B D  Nodules submitted entirely closest margin in cassette C  E  Posterior margin from nodule in cassette D  F I  Ill defined fibrous area from lateral to medial  J  Medial resection margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm breast excision specimen  There are no guide wires in place and no x ray  The outer surface of the specimen is inked in black and it is serially sectioned to reveal uniformly yellow adipose tissue with a scant amount of ill defined white fibrous tissue  There is a small REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white fibrous area along the black inked resection margin  This area is entirely submitted in cassettes K L  Further representative sections are submitted in cassettes M T  Resident  DAVID COON  PhD  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  