c  ragged tissue two possible lymph nodes are identified measuring 1 5cm and 0 7cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Cavity to skin  B D  Cavity  E  Deep margin closest to cavity  F G  Parenchyma from lower outer quadrant  H  Parenchyma from upper outer quadrant  I  Parenchyma from lower inner quadrant  J  Parenchyma from upper inner quadrant  K  Two possible lymph nodes from the lateral aspect  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 20 x 23 x 3cm mastectomy specimen which is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating  superior  and a long stitch designating  lateral   There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm unremarkable tan ellipse of skin with a central 3 3cm nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  No lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  L N  Upper outer quadrant  O P  Lower outer quadrant  Q R  Lower inner quadrant  Q represents deep margin   S U  Upper inner quadrant  S represents deep margin   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional tissue upper outer left breast  is a 8 x 7 x 3cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned and no masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted in V EE  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of adipose tissue within which two lymph nodes are identified measuring 1 5cm and 2 3cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  FF  One whole lymph node  GG  One lymph node bisected  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  MJF      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS D