 simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm nipple areolar complex with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable everted nipple  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a suture indicating 12 o clock  There are also 3 detached fragments of unoriented  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to 13 x 6 x 1 5cm  The anterior surface is inked blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 4 lesional areas  described as follows  Lesion  1 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm firm  tan white mass  with surrounding fibrous tissue  located 3 2cm from the posterior margin  0 7cm from the anterior margin  and 2 1cm directly inferior to the nipple areolar complex  Lesion  2 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm hollowed out area surrounded by firm fibrous tissue  consistent with prior biopsy site  which is located in the superior medial portion of the specimen  2 2cm from the posterior margin  2 4cm from the anterior margin  and 3 6cm directly superiorly to the nipple areolar complex  Lesion  3 is located in the superior portion of the specimen  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of fibrous tissue with rubbery nodularity  which is located 1 1cm from the posterior margin and 3 8cm from the anterior margin  Lesion  4 is located in the medial anterior portion of the specimen  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm area of granular fibrous tissue from which yellow  pasty material is expressed  3 5cm from the posterior margin and 1 4cm from the anterior margin  continuous with an area of fibrous tissue that contains a metal clip  The lateral superior aspect of the specimen is dissected and no definitive lymph nodes are grossly identified  The detached fragments of fibroadipose tissue are inked black and serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable cut surface   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  1  with anterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESS